Falsifies `system_tests::user::x86_port_tests::a_read_only_port_capability_must_not_grant_port_output`.

Architecture: x86_64

The defect is the one milestone 768 (provisional) fixed: `sched::thread_control_block_insert_from`
installs `Thread::port_range_grant` for any `PortRange` capability, whatever its rights. The patch
deletes the `cap.rights.allows(Rights::WRITE)` condition, so a `READ`-only port capability opens the
TSS I/O bitmap again and the child's `out` is permitted.

Expected to fail: `assert_eq!(msg[0], EVENT_FAULT, "a thread whose only PortRange capability lacks
WRITE executed `out` without faulting ...")`, with supervision message `[EVENT_EXIT, ..]`.

Regenerated 2026-10-07 (UTC) by the lane for milestone 779 (fuzz the surface a confined process can
reach), whose capability-spelling pass
renamed `thread_control_block_insert_from`'s bare `cap` local to `capability` (the
cap-abbreviation ratchet, calef 2026-10-06): same condition deleted, same defect.

Regenerated 2026-10-11 (UTC) for milestone 840 (the scheduler file is split along its seams):
the same lines, moved out of `kernel/src/sched.rs` into `kernel/src/sched/thread_control_block.rs` unchanged, so the defect is
the same and only the path and line numbers differ.

diff --git a/kernel/src/sched/thread_control_block.rs b/kernel/src/sched/thread_control_block.rs
index a251ed623..149e5ab53 100644
--- a/kernel/src/sched/thread_control_block.rs
+++ b/kernel/src/sched/thread_control_block.rs
@@ -89,9 +89,7 @@ pub(super) fn thread_control_block_insert_from(
     // delegated later by `SEND_CAP` is not cached. A `PortRange` without `WRITE` grants nothing:
     // the TSS bitmap cannot permit `in` without `out` (§121); the capability still lands.
     #[cfg(target_arch = "x86_64")]
-    if let crate::cap::Object::PortRange(base, count) = capability.object
-        && capability.rights.allows(crate::cap::Rights::WRITE)
-    {
+    if let crate::cap::Object::PortRange(base, count) = capability.object {
         t.port_range_grant = Some((base, count));
     }
     Ok(landed)
